#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:42
msgid "🛠️ Maintenance Overview"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:44
msgid "Why this center exists"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:45
msgid "Every background job (email, CRM, webhooks, attachments) moves through the ContactIn queue. The Maintenance tab lets operators inspect those flows, retrigger stuck work, and keep storage lean without touching the database."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:47
msgid "Use it after outages, credential changes, or deployments that paused cron."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:48
msgid "All actions require the Manage Options capability, so everyday editors cannot run them accidentally."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:49
msgid "Manual processing operations run asynchronously with real-time progress indication—no page blocking."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:50
msgid "Status badges update in real time—refresh the page after taking action to confirm counts drop."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:51
msgid "All recurring cron schedules are created during plugin activation only, preventing duplicate schedules."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:57
msgid "⚡ Queue Recovery"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:59
msgid "Process Email/CRM Pending Now"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:60
msgid "Triggers asynchronous processing of pending email or CRM items without waiting for WP-Cron. Great for clearing a surge of pending emails or CRM syncs right after you fix credentials."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:62
msgid "Processing runs in the background—you can continue working while it completes."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:63
msgid "A progress bar appears showing real-time status with pending counts updating every 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:64
msgid "Progress bar auto-hides 3 seconds after completion."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:65
msgid "CRM processing includes record syncs, attachment retries, and queued CRM deletions in the progress count."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:66
msgid "If counts remain high after completion, move to Completed & Stuck → Reset Processing."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:70
msgid "Reschedule Queue"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:71
msgid "Adjusts the next run time for email or CRM queue processors. Enter the number of seconds until the next run (e.g., 120 for 2 minutes)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:73
msgid "All recurring cron schedules are created during plugin activation only—no runtime scheduling occurs."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:74
msgid "This reschedule operation updates the existing recurring schedule without creating duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:75
msgid "Manual processing triggers single-event execution and does not affect recurring schedules."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:76
msgid "Next run time displays in the card status line so you can confirm the change."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:82
msgid "🧰 Dead Letter Queue & Failed Syncs"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:85
msgid "Retries all failed CRM record syncs, attachment uploads, and deletions that are in retry or DLQ status. Items are processed immediately and the operation provides detailed before/after statistics."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:87
msgid "Run this after fixing CRM credentials, Salesforce authentication, or API issues."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:88
msgid "Success message shows: items retried, and status change for records/files/deletions (e.g., \"↓3\" = 3 fewer failures, \"✓ Cleared\" = all resolved)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:89
msgid "Last retry timestamp displays below the status line showing when the operation last ran and how many failures were resolved."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:90
msgid "If failure counts persist after retry, it means items failed again during processing—check CRM logs for specific API errors."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:91
msgid "\"Retry\" status = pending automatic retry with exponential backoff. \"DLQ\" status = exhausted all retry attempts (dead letter queue)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:95
msgid "Understanding Active Failures"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:96
msgid "The Failed CRM Syncs widget shows \"Active Failures\" which are items currently in retry or DLQ status. These counts represent ongoing issues, not historical records."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:98
msgid "Counts decrease when items succeed, and stay the same or increase if items fail again after retry."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:99
msgid "Successfully completed items are automatically cleaned up daily (see Completed & Stuck section below)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:100
msgid "Hover over the status text to see a tooltip explaining how retry and DLQ counts work."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:101
msgid "Page auto-reloads after retry operations to show updated counts—wait for reload before interpreting results."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:106
msgid "Moves every failed email attempt back to Pending so the queue can reprocess them with the latest credentials and circuit state."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:108
msgid "Run this after fixing SMTP credentials or email configuration issues."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:109
msgid "If items fail again, check the Email logs for the exact SMTP error."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:114
msgid "Permanently deletes failed jobs older than the number of days you specify (0 deletes everything). Helpful when bad data is no longer relevant."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:116
msgid "Record the DLQ count before clearing so auditors know what was removed."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:117
msgid "Use a smaller window (e.g., 30 days) in regulated environments to keep forensic history."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:118
msgid "DLQ items older than 30 days are automatically cleaned up daily by the maintenance cron."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:124
msgid "📦 Completed & Stuck Items"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:126
msgid "Automatic Daily Cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:127
msgid "The system automatically cleans up old queue items every 24 hours via the maintenance cron job. This keeps database tables lean without manual intervention."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:129
msgid "Completed queue items older than 7 days are automatically deleted daily."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:130
msgid "DLQ items older than 30 days are automatically deleted daily."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:131
msgid "Check the ContactIn logs to see cleanup statistics after each daily maintenance run."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:132
msgid "This automatic cleanup ensures retry/DLQ stats show only active failures, not historical ones."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:136
msgid "Manual Clear Completed"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:137
msgid "Manually removes successfully processed jobs older than the threshold you set. Use this if you need immediate cleanup or want a custom retention period."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:139
msgid "Useful for debugging when you want to clear recent completions to see new activity clearly."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:140
msgid "Completed count in the card status line tells you how many items are eligible for cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:141
msgid "Automatic daily cleanup uses 7-day retention; use this for shorter or longer periods as needed."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:145
msgid "Reset Processing → Pending"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:146
msgid "Detects messages stuck in the “processing” state beyond the minutes you enter and moves them back to Pending so the worker can retry."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:148
msgid "Use 5–10 minutes for most hosts; increase if you routinely send large attachments."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:149
msgid "If the same items keep returning to Processing, investigate server CPU limits or third-party rate limits."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:155
msgid "🚦 Circuits & Email"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:158
msgid "Closes open SMTP and CRM circuit breakers after you fix upstream issues. Until reset, related queue delivery stays paused to avoid repeated failures."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:160
msgid "Run this after updating SMTP passwords, Salesforce tokens, or webhook endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:161
msgid "Check the circuit badges at the top—Closed = healthy, Open = tripped."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:165
msgid "Skip Email Items (SMTP Off)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:166
msgid "Marks email work as handled while SMTP is intentionally disabled (legacy email statuses + unified email queue, and clears active email DLQ entries)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:168
msgid "Use during maintenance windows when SMTP is blocked by your host."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:169
msgid "Communicate with stakeholders first—skipped notifications are not resent later."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:175
msgid "🤖 Intent Classification"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:178
msgid "Uses the machine learning classifier to automatically categorize messages that lack intent labels. This is useful after updating classification patterns or following a major inbox migration."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:180
msgid "The counter shows how many messages are currently unclassified across your inbox."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:181
msgid "Classification runs asynchronously—the page displays current intent distribution (e.g., Sales: 45%, Support: 30%, Other: 25%)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:182
msgid "Once complete, the unclassified count will decrease and messages appear with their new intent labels in the inbox."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:183
msgid "If you do not like the automatic classifications, use the Intent Learning widget below to improve patterns."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:189
msgid "🔐 GDPR & CRM Cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:191
msgid "Synced Contacts Ready for Deletion"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:192
msgid "Shows the number of contacts previously synced to your CRM (Salesforce) that are marked for deletion per GDPR requests or bulk cleanup operations."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:194
msgid "Each contact is tracked with a full audit trail—deletion timestamps, sync status, and error logs are retained for compliance."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:199
msgid "Schedules synced contacts for batch processing using the background queue. Recommended for high-volume deletions to avoid blocking the admin interface."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:201
msgid "Deletions go through the unified queue system with automatic retries and exponential backoff."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:202
msgid "Check the CRM Delete badges (Pending, Failed, Deleted) at the top to monitor progress."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:203
msgid "Failed deletions will retry automatically; review CRM logs if deletions remain stuck in DLQ."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:207
msgid "Delete Now (Immediate)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:208
msgid "Processes deletions immediately with full sync logic and fallback handling. Use this when you need a fast resolution to a GDPR deletion request."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:210
msgid "When a CRM endpoint is unavailable, the tool attempts fallback strategies (e.g., mark inactive in Salesforce instead of hard delete)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:211
msgid "All deletion attempts are logged with timestamps and sync status in the GDPR audit log."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:212
msgid "Use the \"View GDPR Log\" button to inspect the full deletion history for a contact."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:218
msgid "🧹 Attachment Cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:220
msgid "When to run a scan"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:221
msgid "Scans the uploads directory for orphaned files—typically created when submissions are deleted or truncated by storage quotas."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:223
msgid "Trigger a scan monthly on busy sites or after bulk inbox cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:224
msgid "Watch the Last Scan timestamp and size summary to estimate impact before deleting."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:228
msgid "Cleaning up safely"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:229
msgid "Use “Clean Up Orphaned Files” once you have reviewed the counts. The tool only deletes files no longer referenced in the database."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:231
msgid "If the button is disabled, no orphaned files were detected in the last scan."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:232
msgid "Download a server backup before deleting large batches in environments without snapshots."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:238
msgid "📚 Intent Learning"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:240
msgid "What is Intent Learning?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:241
msgid "The Intent Learning widget at the bottom allows you to manually train and improve the ML classifier by marking messages with the correct intent category. Over time, the model learns your business patterns and automatically classifies new messages more accurately."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:243
msgid "Select a message from your inbox and mark it with the correct intent (e.g., Sales, Support, Billing, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:244
msgid "The system records your feedback in the learning dataset."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:245
msgid "After collecting enough corrected examples, retrain the classifier using \"Reclassify Unclassified Messages\" to apply improvements."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:246
msgid "View learning history and training statistics in the widget to track model improvement."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:250
msgid "Best practices for training"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:252
msgid "Start with 10-20 correct examples per intent category to establish patterns."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:253
msgid "Regularly review misclassified messages in your inbox and correct them via the learning widget."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:254
msgid "Check the learning statistics monthly to see which categories have sufficient training data."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:255
msgid "The more examples you provide, the more accurate automated classifications become."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:261
msgid "📊 Badges & Status Lines"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:264
msgid "Top badges mirror live queue counts so you never guess which control to use."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:265
msgid "CRM Record, CRM File, and CRM Delete each use a consistent summary: Pending, Synced/Deleted, Failed."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:266
msgid "Circuit badges list each integration (SMTP, CRM, Webhooks). Closed = delivering, Open = paused."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:267
msgid "Each card surfaces the metric that action affects (e.g., DLQ count, next run time, completed totals)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:273
msgid "🩺 Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:275
msgid "Queue never processes"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:277
msgid "Verify WP-Cron is enabled or use a server-side cron to hit wp-cron.php."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:278
msgid "Click “Process Email Pending Now” or “Process CRM Pending Now” and watch Pending badges—if they drop, cron scheduling is the issue."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:282
msgid "DLQ or Retry counts remain high after retry"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:284
msgid "Check the retry success message for before/after stats—persistent counts mean items are failing again, not a display bug."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:285
msgid "Look at \"Last retry\" timestamp below the status line to see if the retry operation actually ran recently."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:286
msgid "Inspect CRM/Email logs for the specific HTTP or SMTP status code causing repeated failures."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:287
msgid "Reset the related circuit breaker after fixing the upstream system, then retry again."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:288
msgid "If the same items repeatedly fail, they may have invalid data (bad email format, missing required CRM fields, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:292
msgid "Cron overlaps or timeouts"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:294
msgid "Use “Reset Processing → Pending” with a low threshold (5 min) to free stuck jobs."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:295
msgid "Reduce batch sizes via plugin filters or ensure the server PHP max execution time is at least 120 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:298
msgid "Intent classifications seem inaccurate"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:300
msgid "Check how many training examples have been collected in the Intent Learning widget."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:301
msgid "Provide at least 10-20 correct examples per intent to improve model accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:302
msgid "Mark misclassified messages as you review them to continuously train the model."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:306
msgid "GDPR deletions stuck in queue or DLQ"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:308
msgid "Verify CRM credentials are still valid by testing a manual record sync."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:309
msgid "Review the CRM logs for specific API errors (e.g., invalid OAuth token, rate limits exceeded)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:310
msgid "Reset the CRM circuit breaker after fixing the issue, then retry the failed deletions."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/partials/maintenance-help-modal.php:311
msgid "If immediate deletion is critical, use the \"Delete Now\" button and check fallback strategy results in the GDPR log."
msgstr ""

